&lt;!-- Click the canvas to reset the tiling and pick a random color scheme from the ones available in config. Change the config object to increase the size or experiment with different color schemes.  --&gt;

&lt;!-- We use an L-System to generate the lines of the Penrose tiling. The logic to compute lines is imported from [this awesome interactive l-system explorer](/@kelleyvanevert/l-systems-2). I've re-written the rendering to work with canvas and paperjs and I've added fill colors to the shapes in the tiling. --&gt;
&lt;!-- ` --&gt;

penroseLSystem = `order: 5
axiom: [N]++[N]++[N]++[N]++[N]
angle: 36
colorful

M -&gt; OF++PF----NF[-OF----MF]++
N -&gt; +OF--PF[---MF--NF]+
O -&gt; -MF++NF[+++OF++PF]-
P -&gt; --OF++++MF[+PF++++NF]--NF
F -&gt;`

